msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.page_title"
msgid "kwtSMS help"
msgstr "kwtSMS help"

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.intro"
msgid "Set up kwtSMS, understand what it costs, and fix delivery problems. Pick a topic."
msgstr "Set up kwtSMS, understand what it costs, and fix delivery problems. Pick a topic."

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.toc"
msgid "Topics"
msgstr "Topics"

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.open_page"
msgid "Open [page]"
msgstr "Open [page]"

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.overview.title"
msgid "What kwtSMS does"
msgstr "What kwtSMS does"

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.overview.p1"
msgid "kwtSMS sends SMS from your store through the kwtSMS gateway. Customers and administrators get a message when an order is placed and when its status changes, in English and Arabic."
msgstr "kwtSMS sends SMS from your store through the kwtSMS gateway. Customers and administrators get a message when an order is placed and when its status changes, in English and Arabic."

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.overview.li1"
msgid "A text for every order status and receiver, in each language, that you edit on the Templates page."
msgstr "A text for every order status and receiver, in each language, that you edit on the Templates page."

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.overview.li2"
msgid "A switch for each message, so nothing goes out until you turn it on."
msgstr "A switch for each message, so nothing goes out until you turn it on."

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.overview.li3"
msgid "Test mode, pilot mode, daily limits, and quiet hours to keep cost and noise under control."
msgstr "Test mode, pilot mode, daily limits, and quiet hours to keep cost and noise under control."

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.overview.li4"
msgid "A dashboard, a log of every message, and a list of administrator numbers for order alerts."
msgstr "A dashboard, a log of every message, and a list of administrator numbers for order alerts."

# 2026-10-22 22:46 +03: Task A8, task 596. Vendor SMS exists in 1.1 (Multi-Vendor), on a number the administrator approves.
msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.overview.p2"
msgid "kwtSMS sends one-way messages, so customers can't reply. In Multi-Vendor, vendors get SMS too, on a number you approve on the Vendor SMS page."
msgstr "kwtSMS sends one-way messages, so customers can't reply. In Multi-Vendor, vendors get SMS too, on a number you approve on the Vendor SMS page."

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.account.title"
msgid "Your kwtSMS account"
msgstr "Your kwtSMS account"

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.account.p1"
msgid "Create an account on the kwtSMS website and buy credits. One credit pays for one SMS page."
msgstr "Create an account on the kwtSMS website and buy credits. One credit pays for one SMS page."

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.account.p2"
msgid "Then turn on API access in your kwtSMS account and create an API username and password. The add-on signs in with them. The API username is not your account mobile number, and the API password is not your store password."
msgstr "Then turn on API access in your kwtSMS account and create an API username and password. The add-on signs in with them. The API username is not your account mobile number, and the API password is not your store password."

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.account.sender_title"
msgid "Sender ID"
msgstr "Sender ID"

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.account.sender_p1"
msgid "The Sender ID is the name customers see as the sender. kwtSMS gives every account KWT-SMS for testing only. It can delay messages and doesn't reach Virgin Kuwait numbers. Register your own Sender ID before you go live."
msgstr "The Sender ID is the name customers see as the sender. kwtSMS gives every account KWT-SMS for testing only. It can delay messages and doesn't reach Virgin Kuwait numbers. Register your own Sender ID before you go live."

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.account.sender_transactional"
msgid "Transactional: for order confirmations and status updates sent to one customer. It reaches numbers on the Do Not Disturb (DND) list. One-time fee: 15 KD."
msgstr "Transactional: for order confirmations and status updates sent to one customer. It reaches numbers on the Do Not Disturb (DND) list. One-time fee: 15 KD."

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.account.sender_promotional"
msgid "Promotional: for offers sent to many people. Messages to DND numbers are blocked, and the credits are still spent. One-time fee: 10 KD."
msgstr "Promotional: for offers sent to many people. Messages to DND numbers are blocked, and the credits are still spent. One-time fee: 10 KD."

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.account.sender_p2"
msgid "Use a transactional Sender ID for order SMS. kwtSMS registers a Sender ID in about 5 working days. The fees above were right when this page was written. The Sender ID help page has the current ones."
msgstr "Use a transactional Sender ID for order SMS. kwtSMS registers a Sender ID in about 5 working days. The fees above were right when this page was written. The Sender ID help page has the current ones."

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.account.intl_title"
msgid "Sending outside Kuwait"
msgstr "Sending outside Kuwait"

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.account.intl_p1"
msgid "International sending is off until you ask kwtSMS to turn it on. Once it is on, bots can place fake orders from other countries and spend your credits fast. Turn on CAPTCHA at checkout before you ask for it."
msgstr "International sending is off until you ask kwtSMS to turn it on. Once it is on, bots can place fake orders from other countries and spend your credits fast. Turn on CAPTCHA at checkout before you ask for it."

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.account.intl_p2"
msgid "kwtSMS also caps international SMS per day. When you reach the cap, the gateway answers ERR035: customers in other countries get no SMS until the next day, Kuwait numbers are not affected, and the add-on shows a notice."
msgstr "kwtSMS also caps international SMS per day. When you reach the cap, the gateway answers ERR035: customers in other countries get no SMS until the next day, Kuwait numbers are not affected, and the add-on shows a notice."

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.account.intl_p3"
msgid "On Settings, choose the countries where customers can get SMS."
msgstr "On Settings, choose the countries where customers can get SMS."

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.setup.title"
msgid "Set up, step by step"
msgstr "Set up, step by step"

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.setup.intro"
msgid "Follow these steps in order. The Dashboard shows which ones are done."
msgstr "Follow these steps in order. The Dashboard shows which ones are done."

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.setup.s1"
msgid "Log in. On Settings, enter your API username and password."
msgstr "Log in. On Settings, enter your API username and password."

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.setup.s2"
msgid "Choose a Sender ID from the list. Don't keep KWT-SMS on a live store."
msgstr "Choose a Sender ID from the list. Don't keep KWT-SMS on a live store."

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.setup.s3"
msgid "Check the default country. A number typed without a country code is read as a number from that country."
msgstr "Check the default country. A number typed without a country code is read as a number from that country."

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.setup.s4"
msgid "Set your SMS brand name on the Templates page. Customers see it at the start of every message."
msgstr "Set your SMS brand name on the Templates page. Customers see it at the start of every message."

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.setup.s5"
msgid "Send a test SMS to your own phone from Settings."
msgstr "Send a test SMS to your own phone from Settings."

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.setup.s6"
msgid "Review the switches and texts on the Templates page, in English and Arabic."
msgstr "Review the switches and texts on the Templates page, in English and Arabic."

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.setup.s7"
msgid "Turn off test mode when you are ready for real messages."
msgstr "Turn off test mode when you are ready for real messages."

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.setup.s8"
msgid "Turn on SMS."
msgstr "Turn on SMS."

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.golive.title"
msgid "Before you go live"
msgstr "Before you go live"

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.golive.intro"
msgid "Check these before customers get real SMS."
msgstr "Check these before customers get real SMS."

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.golive.g1"
msgid "A transactional Sender ID is registered. It takes about 5 working days."
msgstr "A transactional Sender ID is registered. It takes about 5 working days."

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.golive.g2"
msgid "The English and Arabic templates are reviewed."
msgstr "The English and Arabic templates are reviewed."

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.golive.g3"
msgid "Administrator numbers are added on the Admin SMS alerts page."
msgstr "Administrator numbers are added on the Admin SMS alerts page."

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.golive.g4"
msgid "A pilot run with your own numbers worked. Pilot mode sends real SMS only to the administrator numbers and logs the rest."
msgstr "A pilot run with your own numbers worked. Pilot mode sends real SMS only to the administrator numbers and logs the rest."

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.golive.g5"
msgid "Test mode is off, and the test messages that held credits are deleted from your kwtSMS queue."
msgstr "Test mode is off, and the test messages that held credits are deleted from your kwtSMS queue."

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.golive.g6"
msgid "CAPTCHA is on at checkout, so bots can't place fake orders that send SMS."
msgstr "CAPTCHA is on at checkout, so bots can't place fake orders that send SMS."

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.switches.title"
msgid "SMS switches and the Notify boxes"
msgstr "SMS switches and the Notify boxes"

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.switches.intro"
msgid "Three things decide whether an SMS goes out."
msgstr "Three things decide whether an SMS goes out."

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.switches.s1"
msgid "The main switch on Settings. Nothing is sent while SMS are off."
msgstr "The main switch on Settings. Nothing is sent while SMS are off."

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.switches.s2"
msgid "The switch of each message, on the Templates page and on Administration > Notifications. They are the same switches, so a change in one place shows in the other."
msgstr "The switch of each message, on the Templates page and on Administration > Notifications. They are the same switches, so a change in one place shows in the other."

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.switches.s3"
msgid "The Notify boxes on the order page and when you change a status. If you untick Notify for the customer, that customer gets no SMS for that change."
msgstr "The Notify boxes on the order page and when you change a status. If you untick Notify for the customer, that customer gets no SMS for that change."

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.switches.p1"
msgid "After install, only the new order messages for customers and administrators are on. Every status message is off until you turn it on."
msgstr "After install, only the new order messages for customers and administrators are on. Every status message is off until you turn it on."

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.switches.p2"
msgid "The Receivers setting on Administration > Notifications is the list of e-mail recipients. SMS to administrators use the list on the Admin SMS alerts page."
msgstr "The Receivers setting on Administration > Notifications is the list of e-mail recipients. SMS to administrators use the list on the Admin SMS alerts page."

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.ph.title"
msgid "Placeholders"
msgstr "Placeholders"

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.ph.p1"
msgid "Write a placeholder in curly braces, like {order_id}. The add-on replaces it when the message goes out. A message with a placeholder the add-on doesn't know is blocked before sending."
msgstr "Write a placeholder in curly braces, like {order_id}. The add-on replaces it when the message goes out. A message with a placeholder the add-on doesn't know is blocked before sending."

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.ph.col_name"
msgid "Placeholder"
msgstr "Placeholder"

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.ph.col_meaning"
msgid "What it becomes"
msgstr "What it becomes"

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.ph.store_name"
msgid "Your SMS brand name"
msgstr "Your SMS brand name"

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.ph.order_id"
msgid "The order number"
msgstr "The order number"

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.ph.order_ids"
msgid "The order numbers of one checkout: the first three, then how many more (Multi-Vendor)"
msgstr "The order numbers of one checkout: the first three, then how many more (Multi-Vendor)"

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.ph.vendor_name"
msgid "The vendor's name (Multi-Vendor)"
msgstr "The vendor's name (Multi-Vendor)"

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.ph.order_total"
msgid "The order total, in the order's currency"
msgstr "The order total, in the order's currency"

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.ph.currency"
msgid "The currency code, or its Arabic name in Arabic texts"
msgstr "The currency code, or its Arabic name in Arabic texts"

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.ph.order_status"
msgid "The name of the order status"
msgstr "The name of the order status"

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.ph.customer_first_name"
msgid "The customer's first name"
msgstr "The customer's first name"

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.ph.customer_last_name"
msgid "The customer's last name"
msgstr "The customer's last name"

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.ph.order_date"
msgid "The order date"
msgstr "The order date"

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.ph.payment_method"
msgid "The payment method"
msgstr "The payment method"

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.ph.shipping_method"
msgid "The shipping method"
msgstr "The shipping method"

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.costs.title"
msgid "What an SMS costs"
msgstr "What an SMS costs"

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.costs.p1"
msgid "kwtSMS charges one credit for each SMS page. An English page holds [gsm_single] characters. A longer text uses pages of [gsm_multi] characters."
msgstr "kwtSMS charges one credit for each SMS page. An English page holds [gsm_single] characters. A longer text uses pages of [gsm_multi] characters."

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.costs.p2"
msgid "Arabic changes the count. A text with even one Arabic letter, or any other character outside the English set, becomes Unicode. A page then holds only [unicode_single] characters, or [unicode_multi] when there is more than one page. The same text can need two or three times as many pages."
msgstr "Arabic changes the count. A text with even one Arabic letter, or any other character outside the English set, becomes Unicode. A page then holds only [unicode_single] characters, or [unicode_multi] when there is more than one page. The same text can need two or three times as many pages."

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.costs.p3"
msgid "A long brand name works the same way: it takes characters from every message. Keep your SMS brand name short, and in English letters if your texts are English. A customer's name can also turn an English SMS into Unicode when it is written in Arabic."
msgstr "A long brand name works the same way: it takes characters from every message. Keep your SMS brand name short, and in English letters if your texts are English. A customer's name can also turn an English SMS into Unicode when it is written in Arabic."

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.costs.p4"
msgid "A message can have at most [max_pages] pages. The Templates page shows the page count of every text as you type, and the worst case."
msgstr "A message can have at most [max_pages] pages. The Templates page shows the page count of every text as you type, and the worst case."

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.costs.low_title"
msgid "Know when credits run low"
msgstr "Know when credits run low"

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.costs.low_p1"
msgid "The Dashboard shows your balance and warns you when it runs low. Also turn on the low-balance notification in your kwtSMS account, so you hear about it when you are not in the store. At zero credits, customer SMS stop."
msgstr "The Dashboard shows your balance and warns you when it runs low. Also turn on the low-balance notification in your kwtSMS account, so you hear about it when you are not in the store. At zero credits, customer SMS stop."

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.cron.title"
msgid "Cron: sending queued SMS"
msgstr "Cron: sending queued SMS"

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.cron.p1"
msgid "Some SMS wait in a queue: status updates held for quiet hours, and messages kwtSMS couldn't take yet. A cron job sends them. It also syncs your account once a day and cleans old logs."
msgstr "Some SMS wait in a queue: status updates held for quiet hours, and messages kwtSMS couldn't take yet. A cron job sends them. It also syncs your account once a day and cleans old logs."

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.cron.p2"
msgid "Add this line to the crontab of the user that runs your web server. It runs every minute."
msgstr "Add this line to the crontab of the user that runs your web server. It runs every minute."

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.cron.p3"
msgid "The line is made for this store from its folder and its admin script ([script]). If cron can't find php, write the full path of the PHP command line program instead of php. In /etc/cron.d, put the user name after the five time fields."
msgstr "The line is made for this store from its folder and its admin script ([script]). If cron can't find php, write the full path of the PHP command line program instead of php. In /etc/cron.d, put the user name after the five time fields."

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.cron.p4"
msgid "Without cron, opening the Dashboard sends up to 20 waiting SMS and runs the daily sync if the last sync is old. This happens for any administrator who opens it, including one who can only view it. It is a fallback for stores without a working cron. Nothing is sent while nobody opens the Dashboard, so the real fix is the cron line above."
msgstr "Without cron, opening the Dashboard sends up to 20 waiting SMS and runs the daily sync if the last sync is old. This happens for any administrator who opens it, including one who can only view it. It is a fallback for stores without a working cron. Nothing is sent while nobody opens the Dashboard, so the real fix is the cron line above."

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.cron.url_title"
msgid "No crontab? Use the URL"
msgstr "No crontab? Use the URL"

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.cron.url_p1"
msgid "Some hosts only offer a URL cron. Turn on the cron URL on Settings, copy the key shown there, and call this address every minute. Replace YOUR_CRON_KEY with that key."
msgstr "Some hosts only offer a URL cron. Turn on the cron URL on Settings, copy the key shown there, and call this address every minute. Replace YOUR_CRON_KEY with that key."

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.cron.url_p2"
msgid "The URL takes POST requests only. Send the key in the header X-Kwtsms-Cron-Key and never in the address, because servers log addresses. Any other request is refused. A good call answers {\"ok\":true}."
msgstr "The URL takes POST requests only. Send the key in the header X-Kwtsms-Cron-Key and never in the address, because servers log addresses. Any other request is refused. A good call answers {\"ok\":true}."

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.cron.url_off"
msgid "The cron URL is off on this store. It is off until you turn it on."
msgstr "The cron URL is off on this store. It is off until you turn it on."

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.cron.url_on"
msgid "The cron URL is on."
msgstr "The cron URL is on."

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.cron.timeout_title"
msgid "A 504 error is not always a failure"
msgstr "A 504 error is not always a failure"

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.cron.timeout_p1"
msgid "Some proxies and hosts cut a request after 60 seconds and show a 504 error, although the run keeps going and finishes. Check Cron last ran on the Dashboard before you decide the run failed."
msgstr "Some proxies and hosts cut a request after 60 seconds and show a 504 error, although the run keeps going and finishes. Check Cron last ran on the Dashboard before you decide the run failed."

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.cron.lock_title"
msgid "Two runs at once"
msgstr "Two runs at once"

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.cron.lock_p1"
msgid "Runs should not overlap. The add-on uses the core lock for that, and the lock works only when lock_backend is database or redis. With lock_backend set to dummy there is no mutual exclusion: two runs can overlap. Set lock_backend in config.local.php."
msgstr "Runs should not overlap. The add-on uses the core lock for that, and the lock works only when lock_backend is database or redis. With lock_backend set to dummy there is no mutual exclusion: two runs can overlap. Set lock_backend in config.local.php."

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.cron.lock_state"
msgid "This store uses lock_backend [backend]."
msgstr "This store uses lock_backend [backend]."

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.cron.lock_ok"
msgid "That gives mutual exclusion: only one run works at a time."
msgstr "That gives mutual exclusion: only one run works at a time."

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.cron.lock_bad"
msgid "That gives no mutual exclusion. Change it to database or redis."
msgstr "That gives no mutual exclusion. Change it to database or redis."

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.test.title"
msgid "Test mode and held credits"
msgstr "Test mode and held credits"

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.test.p1"
msgid "Test mode is on after install. Every message then goes to kwtSMS as a test: kwtSMS accepts it and never delivers it."
msgstr "Test mode is on after install. Every message then goes to kwtSMS as a test: kwtSMS accepts it and never delivers it."

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.test.p2"
msgid "Each test message still holds credits in your kwtSMS queue until you delete it. Delete them at kwtsms.com > Account > Queue to get the credits back. The Dashboard shows how many credits are held."
msgstr "Each test message still holds credits in your kwtSMS queue until you delete it. Delete them at kwtsms.com > Account > Queue to get the credits back. The Dashboard shows how many credits are held."

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.test.p3"
msgid "Turn test mode off on Settings when you are ready for real messages. If the Sender ID is still KWT-SMS, you must confirm first."
msgstr "Turn test mode off on Settings when you are ready for real messages. If the Sender ID is still KWT-SMS, you must confirm first."

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.ip.title"
msgid "IP restrictions and proxies"
msgstr "IP restrictions and proxies"

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.ip.p1"
msgid "kwtSMS can accept API calls only from the IP addresses you list. If your server's address is not on the list, kwtSMS answers ERR024 and the add-on pauses sending."
msgstr "kwtSMS can accept API calls only from the IP addresses you list. If your server's address is not on the list, kwtSMS answers ERR024 and the add-on pauses sending."

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.ip.p2"
msgid "Ask your host for the server's public outgoing IP, add it in the API settings of your kwtSMS account, then select Retry now on Settings."
msgstr "Ask your host for the server's public outgoing IP, add it in the API settings of your kwtSMS account, then select Retry now on Settings."

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.ip.p3"
msgid "ERR034 means kwtSMS sees your server's address as a proxy or VPN. Ask your host for the server's public outgoing IP. If kwtSMS still blocks it, contact kwtSMS support with that address."
msgstr "ERR034 means kwtSMS sees your server's address as a proxy or VPN. Ask your host for the server's public outgoing IP. If kwtSMS still blocks it, contact kwtSMS support with that address."

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.missing.title"
msgid "Message not received"
msgstr "Message not received"

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.missing.intro"
msgid "Work through these steps in order before you contact support."
msgstr "Work through these steps in order before you contact support."

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.missing.s1"
msgid "Check the queue at kwtsms.com > Account > Queue. A message here was accepted but not sent on. Delete it to get its credits back. Bad language, spam filters, and wrong formats are common causes."
msgstr "Check the queue at kwtsms.com > Account > Queue. A message here was accepted but not sent on. Delete it to get its credits back. Bad language, spam filters, and wrong formats are common causes."

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.missing.s2"
msgid "Check that test mode is off. Test messages are never delivered. In the add-on log they carry a TEST badge."
msgstr "Check that test mode is off. Test messages are never delivered. In the add-on log they carry a TEST badge."

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.missing.s3"
msgid "Check the archive at kwtsms.com > Account > Archive. A message in the archive left kwtSMS for the mobile network. A message that is not there was never sent, so look for its error in the add-on log. Kuwait networks send no delivery reports, so the archive is the last proof kwtSMS can give you."
msgstr "Check the archive at kwtsms.com > Account > Archive. A message in the archive left kwtSMS for the mobile network. A message that is not there was never sent, so look for its error in the add-on log. Kuwait networks send no delivery reports, so the archive is the last proof kwtSMS can give you."

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.missing.s4"
msgid "Check the number. Open the message in the archive. The number must be a mobile number in international format, for example 96598765432."
msgstr "Check the number. Open the message in the archive. The number must be a mobile number in international format, for example 96598765432."

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.missing.s5"
msgid "Check Do Not Disturb. Some customers ask their network to block promotional messages. A promotional Sender ID, and KWT-SMS, can't reach them. A transactional Sender ID can."
msgstr "Check Do Not Disturb. Some customers ask their network to block promotional messages. A promotional Sender ID, and KWT-SMS, can't reach them. A transactional Sender ID can."

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.missing.s6"
msgid "Wait a few minutes. KWT-SMS is slow, especially on busy days. Give a message 3 to 5 minutes before you decide it is lost, and use your own Sender ID."
msgstr "Wait a few minutes. KWT-SMS is slow, especially on busy days. Give a message 3 to 5 minutes before you decide it is lost, and use your own Sender ID."

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.missing.s7"
msgid "Still missing? Contact kwtSMS support as described below."
msgstr "Still missing? Contact kwtSMS support as described below."

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.support.title"
msgid "Contact kwtSMS support"
msgstr "Contact kwtSMS support"

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.support.p1"
msgid "If the steps above don't help, contact kwtSMS support. On the Logs page, open the message and select Copy details for kwtSMS support. Paste the result into your message."
msgstr "If the steps above don't help, contact kwtSMS support. On the Logs page, open the message and select Copy details for kwtSMS support. Paste the result into your message."

msgctxt "Languages::kwtsms.help.support.p2"
msgid "It holds what support asks for: your API username, the message ID, the Kuwait date and time, the Sender ID, the numbers, the text, the test flag, and the error code. It never holds your password."
msgstr "It holds what support asks for: your API username, the message ID, the Kuwait date and time, the Sender ID, the numbers, the text, the test flag, and the error code. It never holds your password."

